          %h2#ManifoldsAndOrdbifolds
            %strong Manifolds and orbifolds
          %p
            In the discussion at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+smooth+sets"} geometry of physics – smooth sets
            we have started with very simple model spaces for
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+geometry"} differential geometry
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+spaces"} Cartesian spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+topos"} sheaf topos
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            that they form, very general
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+spaces"} smooth spaces
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
            form a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            for these general
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+sets"} smooth sets
            and hence sit in between the very simple model spaces and the very general smooth sets.
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CartSp
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi SmoothMfd
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi Smooth
                  %mn 0
                  %mi Type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  CartSp \hookrightarrow SmoothMfd \hookrightarrow Smooth0Type
          %p
            In making this statement, we assumed that we already know what smooth manifolds are. Here now we consider the question of
            %em characterizing
            smooth manifolds as special smooth sets, hence (re-)defining them, but in a way that is slightly (though not much) different from the traditional textbook description, a way that is true to the spirit of regarding smooth sets as the good ambient context for doing differential geometry.
          %p
            Or rather, as throughout these notes, by characterizing smooth manifolds among smooth sets in a neat general abstract way, we may carry this characterization verbatim from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+sets"} smooth sets
            to the more general context of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+homotopy+types"} smooth homotopy types
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+groupoids"} smooth groupoids
            comes out as the concept of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+groupoid"} étale groupoid
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiable+stack"} differentiable
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+stack"} étale stack
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifolds"} orbifolds
            the direct analog in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+geometry"} differential geometry
            of what in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+geometry"} algebraic geometry
            is famous as
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Deligne-Mumford+stacks"} Deligne-Mumford stacks
          %p
            Fully generally, the interpretation of the abstract concept of manifold in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+homotopy+types"} smooth homotopy types
            is a concept of
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                smooth
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} étale ∞-groupoids
          %p
            In fact more is true. The terminology
            %em
              smooth
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+groupoid"} étale groupoid
            without further qualification refers to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+groupoids"} smooth groupoids
            that are
            %em locally diffeomorphic
            to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
            here with any other
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+object"} group object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+sets"} smooth sets
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+group"} smooth group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-group"} ∞-group
            object in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+homotopy+types"} smooth homotopy types
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+%E2%88%9E-group"} smooth ∞-group
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/V-manifold"} V-manifold
            is a smooth homotopy type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            which is locally diffeomorphic to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            in a suitable sense. One may say that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is
            %em étalé
            (spread out), but over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
          %p
            For instance in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+Cartan+geometry"} higher
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Cartan+geometry"} super Cartan geometry
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            is typically an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+super+Minkowski+spacetime"} extended super Minkowski spacetime
            (some super
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-group"} n-group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superspacetime"} superspacetime
            locally diffeomorphic to that.
          %p
            A key aspect featured by
            = succeed "-manifolds," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/frame+bundle"} frame bundle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+linear+group"} general linear group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(V)
            – which in the generality of higher differential geometry we define to be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+%E2%88%9E-group"} automorphism ∞-group
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+neighbourhood"} infinitesimal neighbourhood
            of the neutral element in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            are twisted with respect to each other as one moves around on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            This is the key to formulating genuine geometric structure on smooth spaces: following an insight that goes back to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%89lie+Cartan"} Élie Cartan
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integrable+G-structure"}> infinitesimally integrable
            )
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-structure"} G-structure
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduction+of+the+structure+group"} reduction of the structure group
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/frame+bundle"} frame bundle
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "-)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudo-Riemannian+geometry"} pseudo
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+geometry"} Riemannian geometric structure
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+structure"} complex structure
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+structure"} symplectic structure
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+structure"} conformal structure
            and much more. These geometric structures on higher manifolds are the topic of the chapter
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+G-structure+and+Cartan+geometry"} geometry of physics – G-structure and Cartan geometry
          %h3#ModelLayer Model Layer
          %h4#ModelLayerManifolds Manifolds
          %p We give first an account of the traditional definition of smooth manifolds, but (re-)phrasing it equivalently in category-theoretic terms that lend themselves to generalization.
          %h5#FormalSmoothCartesianSpaces Formal smooth Cartesian spaces
          %ol
            %li
          %p
            In order to speak about
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+vectors"} tangent vectors
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+diffeomorphisms"} local diffeomorphisms
            in a way that generalizes to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+differential+geometry"} higher differential geometry
            %em co-represent
            tangent vectors: where a smooth path in a Cartesian space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a smooth function out of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+line"} real line
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            into
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+vector"} tangent vector
            as traditionally defined is intuitively the restriction of such a map to the first order
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+neighbourhood"} infinitesimal neighbourhood
            of the origin in
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
          %p
            The idea now (which is the idea of
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/synthetic+differential+geometry"} synthetic differential geometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+neighbourhood"} infinitesimal neighbourhood
            exists
            %em literally
            as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject"} subobject
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔻
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{D} \hookrightarrow \mathbb{R}
            %em literally
            a morphism
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔻
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{D} \to X
          %p
            In order to see what these generalized Cartesian spaces might be, recall a basic fact about
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
          %p
            Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi CAlg
                    %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CAlg_{\mathbb{R}}
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+algebras"} commutative algebras
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SmoothCartSp"} SmoothCartSp
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+spaces"} Cartesian spaces
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
            between them.
          #EmbeddingOfSmoothManifoldsIntoFormalDualsOfRAlgebras.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi SmoothCartSp
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msubsup
                      %mi CAlg
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C^\infty(-) \colon SmoothCartSp \longrightarrow CAlg_{\mathbb{R}}^{op}
            %p
              which sends a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
              to (the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+dual"} formal dual
              of) its
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+algebra"} algebra
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} full and faithful functor
            %p
              In other words, for two
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+spaces"} Cartesian spaces
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X,Y
              there is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+bijection"} natural bijection
              between the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to Y
              and the algebra homomorphisms
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ←
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(X)\leftarrow C^\infty(Y)
          %p
            See at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/embedding+of+smooth+manifolds+into+formal+duals+of+R-algebras"} embedding of smooth manifolds into formal duals of R-algebras
            for more on this.
          #CarefulWithSmoothAlgebras.num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              One has to be careful that prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EmbeddingOfSmoothManifoldsIntoFormalDualsOfRAlgebras"}
              might seem to imply more than it does. In order that all constructions on all commutative algebras have the desired dual effect on formally dual smooth spaces (e.g. construction of
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/products"} products
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproducts"} coproducts
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K%C3%A4hler+differentials"} Kähler differentials
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
              to
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+algebras"} smooth algebras
          %p
            With Cartesian spaces embedded into the larger context of formal duals of commutative algebras by prop.
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EmbeddingOfSmoothManifoldsIntoFormalDualsOfRAlgebras"}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+spaces"} infinitesimal spaces
            of sorts, and since, via the embedding of prop.
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EmbeddingOfSmoothManifoldsIntoFormalDualsOfRAlgebras"}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+of+functions"} algebra of functions
            it carries, we need to specify those commutative algebras that behave like algebras of functions on infinitesimal Cartesian spaces. The intuition is that these spaces are so small, that the canonical coordinate functions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x^i
            on them take values which are so very small
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} llt
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \llt 1
            that when taken to some power they vanish not only approximately, but identically. But this intuition is easily formalized:
          #FormalSmoothCartesianSpaces.num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p Write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi InfPoint
                    %mo ↪
                    %msubsup
                      %mi CAlg
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    InfPoint \hookrightarrow CAlg_{\mathbb{R}}^{op}
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite category
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+algebras"} commutative algebras
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
              on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+duals"} formal duals
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+algebras"} commutative algebras
              over the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
              of the form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}\oplus V
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              a finite-dimensional
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nilpotent+ideal"} nilpotent ideal
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+Artin+algebras"} local Artin algebras
              over the real numbers). We call this the category of
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimally+thickened+points"} infinitesimally thickened points
            %p Write moreover
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi FormalSmoothCartSp
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi CartSp
                    %mo ⋊
                    %mi InfPoint
                    %mo ↪
                    %msubsup
                      %mi CAlg
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    FormalSmoothCartSp
                    \\coloneqq
                    CartSp \rtimes InfPoint \hookrightarrow CAlg_{\mathbb{R}}^{op}
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+duals"} formal duals
              of those algebras which are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+products"} tensor products
              of commutative
              = succeed "-algebras" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^n) \otimes C^\infty(D)
            %p
              of algebras
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^p)
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
              as in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EmbeddingOfSmoothManifoldsIntoFormalDualsOfRAlgebras"}
              with algebras corresponding to infinitesimally thickened points
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              as above.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              The basic idea of prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FormalSmoothCartesianSpaces"}
              is familiar in
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+geometry"} algebraic geometry
              = succeed "\u2018s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Grothendieck"} Alexander Grothendieck
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crystalline+cohomology"} crystalline cohomology
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+schemes"} formal schemes
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+ringed+spaces"} locally ringed spaces
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ind-objects"} ind-objects
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+geometry"} algebraic geometry
              but also works in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+geometry"} differential geometry
              has been highlighted by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Lawvere"} William Lawvere
              in the 1960s, who phrased it in terms of what is now known as the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kock-Lawvere+axioms"} Kock-Lawvere axioms
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/synthetic+differential+geometry"} synthetic differential geometry
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+algebras"} smooth algebras
              with infinitesimals, but as long as one does not insist on all geometric operations to have algebraic duals, see remark
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CarefulWithSmoothAlgebras"}
              above, then using just plain real algebras with nilpotent elements as done here is sufficient.
          #SmoothCartSpCoreflectiveInFormalSmoothCartSp.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              The evident
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              inclusion of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+Cartesian+spaces"} smooth Cartesian spaces
              into
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+smooth+manifold"} formal smooth Cartesian spaces
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FormalSmoothCartesianSpaces"}
              is
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coreflective+subcategory"} coreflective
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi SmoothCartSp
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mi p
                      %mover
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi i
                    %mi FormalSmoothCartSp
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (i \dashv p)
                    \\;\colon\;
                    SmoothCartSp
                    \\stackrel{\overset{i}{\hookrightarrow}}{\underset{p}{\longleftarrow}}
                    FormalSmoothCartSp
                    \\,.
            %p
              On formal dual algebras,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              is given by quotienting out the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nilpotent+ideal"} nilpotent ideal
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              We need to check that for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi n
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi n
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n_1, n_2 \in \mathbb{N}
              and for all
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi InfPoint
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D \in InfPoint
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+bijection"} natural bijection
              between the set of morphisms
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 1
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 2
                    %mo ×
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{R}^{n_1} \longrightarrow \mathbb{R}^{n_2}\times D
            %p
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi FormalSmoothCartSp
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} FormalSmoothCartSp
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 1
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{R}^{n_1} \longrightarrow \mathbb{R}^{n_2}
            %p
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi SmoothCartSp
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SmoothCartSp
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟵
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi ℝ
                    %mi V
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^{n_1})
                    \\longleftarrow
                    C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^{n_2})\otimes_{\mathbb{R}} V
                    \\,,
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nilpotent+ideal"} nilpotent ideal
              of the formal dual algebra of functions on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            %p
              Now for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
              an element in the algebra on the right which is nilpotent, hence for which there is
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \in \mathbb{N}
              such that
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi v
                        %mi p
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v^p = 0
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
              needs to preserve this condition, hence also
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi v
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi p
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi(v)^p = 0
              and hence also
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi(v)
              is nilpotent. But the only nilpotent element in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^{n_1})
              is zero. Therefore every algebra homomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
              as above has to have
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              in its
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel"} kernel
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi n
                            %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi ℝ
                      %mi V
                      %mo →
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi n
                            %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^{n_2})\otimes_{\mathbb{R}} V \to C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^{n_2})
            %p
              With this the statement follows by prop.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EmbeddingOfSmoothManifoldsIntoFormalDualsOfRAlgebras"}
            %p
              (A similar argument gives that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              is a functor in the first place.)
          %h5#FormalSmoothSets Formal smooth sets
          %p
            Following closely the theory at
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+smooth+sets"} geometry of physics – smooth sets
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+smooth+spaces"} generalized smooth spaces
            which are
            %em locally probe-able
            by the formal smooth Cartesian spaces of def.
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FormalSmoothCartesianSpaces"}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaves"} sheaves
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi FormalSmoothCartSp
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} FormalSmoothCartSp
            that the latter form.
          #FormalSmoothCartesianSpacesSite.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              Regard the category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi FormalSmoothCartSp
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} FormalSmoothCartSp
              of def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FormalSmoothCartesianSpaces"}
              as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
              by equipping it with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coverage"} coverage
              whose covering families are of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo ×
                      %mi D
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi ϕ
                            %mi i
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi id
                            %mi D
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi U
                      %mo ×
                      %mi D
                      %mo }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left\{
                    U_i \times D \stackrel{(\phi_i,id_D)}{\longrightarrow} U \times D
                    \\right\}
            %p
              for
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi SmoothCartSp
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi FormalSmoothCartSp
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U, U_i \in SmoothCartSp \hookrightarrow FormalSmoothCartSp
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi InfPoint
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi FormalSmoothCartSp
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D \in InfPoint \hookrightarrow FormalSmoothCartSp
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mi i
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \stackrel{\phi_i}{\to} U\}
              a covering family in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi SmoothCartSp
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SmoothCartSp
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
          #ToposOfFormalSmoothSets.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              A
              %em formal smooth set
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
              on the site
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi FormalSmoothCartSp
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} FormalSmoothCartSp
              of def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FormalSmoothCartesianSpacesSite"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi FormalSmooth
                    %mn 0
                    %mi Type
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi FormalSmoothCartSp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    FormalSmooth0Type \coloneqq Sh(FormalSmoothCartSp)
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+sheaves"} category of sheaves
              on that site.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              The category of def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ToposOfFormalSmoothSets"}
              is traditionally known as the
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cahiers+topos"} Cahiers topos
          #AdjointQuadrupleOnFormalSmoothSets.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              The co-reflective inclusion of sites of prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SmoothCartSpCoreflectiveInFormalSmoothCartSp"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SmoothCartSp
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mi p
                      %mover
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi i
                    %mi FormalSmoothCartSp
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    SmoothCartSp \stackrel{\overset{i}{\hookrightarrow}}{\underset{p}{\longleftarrow}} FormalSmoothCartSp
            %p
              extends via
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+extension"} Kan extension
              to an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+quadruple"} adjoint quadruple
              of functors
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Smooth
                    %mn 0
                    %mi Type
                    %mover
                      %mover
                        %mover
                          %munder
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mrow
                              %msup
                                %mi i
                                %mo !
                          %mover
                            %mo ↪
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi i
                                %mo *
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟵
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi i
                              %mo *
                      %mover
                        %mo ↪
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi i
                            %mo !
                    %mi FormalSmooth
                    %mn 0
                    %mi Type
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Smooth0Type
                    \\stackrel{\overset{i_!}{\hookrightarrow}}{\stackrel{\overset{i^\ast}{\longleftarrow}}{\stackrel{\overset{i_\ast}{\hookrightarrow}}{\underset{i^!}{\longrightarrow}}}}
                    FormalSmooth0Type
            %p
              between
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+sets"} smooth sets
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+smooth+sets"} formal smooth sets
          %p We agree that when in the following we write an unlabeled inclusion
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Smooth
                  %mn 0
                  %mi Type
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi FormalSmooth
                  %mn 0
                  %mi Type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Smooth0Type \hookrightarrow FormalSmooth0Type
          %p
            then we always mean inclusion by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi i
                    %mo !
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_!
            in the above, not by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_\ast
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            of smooth Cartesian spaces into Cartesian spaces.
          #AdjointTripleOnFormalSmoothSets.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p We write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℜ
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi ℑ
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi &amp;
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi FormalSmooth
                    %mn 0
                    %mi Type
                    %mover
                      %mover
                        %munder
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi i
                              %mo !
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟵
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi i
                              %mo *
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi i
                            %mo *
                    %mi Smooth
                    %mn 0
                    %mi Type
                    %mover
                      %mover
                        %munder
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi i
                              %mo *
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟵
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi i
                              %mo *
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi i
                            %mo !
                    %mi FormalSmooth
                    %mn 0
                    %mi Type
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\Re \dashv \Im \dashv \&amp;)
                    \\;\colon\;
                    FormalSmooth0Type
                    \\stackrel{\overset{i^\ast}{\longrightarrow}}{\stackrel{\overset{i_\ast}{\longleftarrow}}{\underset{i^!}{\longrightarrow}}}
                    Smooth0Type
                    \\stackrel{\overset{i_!}{\longrightarrow}}{\stackrel{\overset{i^\ast}{\longleftarrow}}{\underset{i_\ast}{\longrightarrow}}}
                    FormalSmooth0Type
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+triple"} adjoint triple
              of (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comonad"}> co
              \-)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monads"} monads
              induced from the functors in prop.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AdjointQuadrupleOnFormalSmoothSets"}
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℜ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Re
                  –
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduction+modality"} reduction modality
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℑ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Im
                  –
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+shape+modality"} infinitesimal shape modality
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi &amp;
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \&amp;
                  –
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+flat+modality"} infinitesimal flat modality
          #NatureOfTheModalitiesOnCahiersTopos.num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              The single key fact to understand the operations in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AdjointTripleOnFormalSmoothSets"}
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+Kan+extension"} left Kan extension
              of presheaves along a functor between sites restricts to that functor on representables. (See at
              = succeed ")." do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "Kan+extension#LeftKanOnRepresentables"} Kan extension – Left Kan extension on representables
            %p
              This means that for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi SmoothCartSp
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi FormalSmoothCartSp
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \in SmoothCartSp \hookrightarrow FormalSmoothCartSp
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi InfPoint
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi FormalSmoothCartSp
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D \in InfPoint \hookrightarrow FormalSmoothCartSp
              then
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℜ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi U
                        %mo ×
                        %mi D
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≃
                        %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Re( U \times D) \simeq D
                  ;
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Hom
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi U
                        %mo ×
                        %mi D
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ℑ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≃
                        %mi Hom
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi U
                        %mo ,
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(U \times D, \Im(X)) \simeq Hom(U, X)
                  \.
          %h5#TangentVectors Tangent vectors
          %p The following is the key observation regarding generally the role of nilpotent elements in function algebras and specifically as to the nature of formal Cartesian spaces.
          #TangentVectorsByAlgebra.num_example
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %p
              Write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔻
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{D}
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+dual"} formal dual
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+of+dual+numbers"} algebra of dual numbers
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ϵ
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbb{R}[\epsilon])/(\epsilon^2)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo ×
                    %mi 𝔻
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{R}^n \times \mathbb{D}\longrightarrow \mathbb{R}^n
            %p
              which are the identity after restriction along
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                      %mo →
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                      %mo ×
                      %mi 𝔻
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n \to \mathbb{R}^n \times \mathbb{D}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mi ϵ
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟵
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^n) \oplus \epsilon C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^n))
                    \\longleftarrow
                    C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^n)
            %p
              which are the identity modulo
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϵ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \in C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^n)
              to
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi ϵ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f + (\partial f) \epsilon
            %p
              for some smooth function
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\partial f) \in C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^n)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_1,f_2 \in C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^n)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 2
                    %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo ∂
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 2
                    %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo ∂
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (f_1 f_2 + (\partial (f_1 f_2))\epsilon )
                    \=
                    (f_1 + (\partial f_1) \epsilon)
                    (f_2 + (\partial f_2) \epsilon)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Multiplying this out and using that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon^2 = 0
              this in turn is equivalent to
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo ∂
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 2
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo ∂
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\partial(f_1 f_2) = (\partial f_1) f_2 + f_1 (\partial f_2)
                    \\,.
            %p
              This in turn means equivalently that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial\colon C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^n)\to C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^n)
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivation"} derivation
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
              are equivalent to
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+fields"} vector fields
              = succeed ")." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivations+of+smooth+functions+are+vector+fields"} derivations of smooth functions are vector fields
            %p In particular one finds that maps
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔻
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{D} \longrightarrow \mathbb{R}^n
            %p
              are equivalently single
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+vectors"} tangent vectors
          %p
            Based on this, the following is a classical fact of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/synthetic+differential+geometry"} synthetic differential geometry
          #TangentBundlesAsInternalHoms.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi SmoothMfd
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Smooth
                    %mn 0
                    %mi Type
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi FormalSmooth
                    %mn 0
                    %mi Type
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in SmoothMfd \hookrightarrow Smooth0Type \hookrightarrow FormalSmooth0Type
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi 𝔻
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\mathbb{D},X]
              out of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+interval"} infinitesimal interval
              is equivalent to the total space manifold of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundle"} tangent bundle
              of
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mi X
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi 𝔻
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    T X \simeq [\mathbb{D},X]
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              By definition of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              then morphisms
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi 𝔻
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    U \longrightarrow [\mathbb{D},X]
            %p
              are in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+bijection"} natural bijection
              with morphisms
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ×
                    %mi 𝔻
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    U \times \mathbb{D}\longrightarrow X
                    \\,.
            %p
              By example
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TangentVectorsByAlgebra"}
              these are smoothly
              = succeed "-parameterized" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi T
                    %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    U \longrightarrow T X
                    \\,.
            %p
              Hence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi 𝔻
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\mathbb{D},X]
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T X
              represent isomorphic
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functors"} representable functors
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
              implies that they are themselves
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphic
          %h5#local_diffeomorphisms Local diffeomorphisms
          %p
            The traditional definition of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+diffeomorphisms"} local diffeomorphisms
            says
          #LocalDiffeomorphismTraditional.num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \longrightarrow Y
              between
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
              is a
              %em local diffeomorphism
              if for all points
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\in X
              its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivatives"} derivatives
              at that point induce an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundle"} tangent
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+spaces"} vector spaces
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo ∀
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi d
                    %mi f
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mi x
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi Y
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\underset{x \in X}{\forall} \;\; d f \;\colon\; T_x X \stackrel{\simeq}{\longrightarrow} T_{f(x)}Y
                    \\,.
          %p
            A more
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theoretic
            way to say this, which may still be found in some traditional textbooks, is this
          #LocalDiffeosDetectedByPullbackOfTangentBundle.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_5 Proposition
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \longrightarrow Y
              between
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %em local diffeomorphism
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocalDiffeomorphismTraditional"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundles"} tangent bundles
              that it induces
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi T
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi d
                                  %mi f
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi T
                            %mi Y
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    T X &amp;\stackrel{}{\longrightarrow}&amp; X
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{d f}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    T Y &amp;\stackrel{}{\longrightarrow}&amp; Y
                    }
            %p
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              diagram.
          %p Now this in turn we may further reformulate as follows:
          #TraditionalLocalDiffeosByModality.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_6 Proposition
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \longrightarrow Y
              between
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %em local diffeomorphism
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocalDiffeomorphismTraditional"}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Smooth
                      %mn 0
                      %mi Type
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi FormalSmooth
                      %mn 0
                      %mi Type
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Smooth0Type \hookrightarrow FormalSmooth0Type
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+a+monad"} unit
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} naturality square
              of the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+shape+modality"} infinitesimal shape modality
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AdjointTripleOnFormalSmoothSets"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℑ
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi ℑ
                                  %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℑ
                            %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X &amp;\stackrel{}{\longrightarrow}&amp; \Im X
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{f}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\Im f}}
                    \\\
                    Y &amp;\stackrel{}{\longrightarrow}&amp; \Im Y
                    }
            %p
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              Pullbacks of sheaves are detected by giving pullbacks of sets after evaluating on all possible objects of the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            %p
              Consider first those objects of the form
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi SmoothCartSp
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi FormalSmoothCartSp
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi FormalSmooth
                      %mn 0
                      %mi Type
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \in SmoothCartSp \hookrightarrow FormalSmoothCartSp \hookrightarrow FormalSmooth0Type
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#NatureOfTheModalitiesOnCahiersTopos"}
              for these the diagram in question becomes
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Hom
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi U
                            %mo ,
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi id
                          %mtd
                            %mi Hom
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi U
                            %mo ,
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi Hom
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi U
                                  %mo ,
                                  %mi f
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi Hom
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi U
                                  %mo ,
                                  %mi f
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Hom
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi U
                            %mo ,
                            %mi Y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi id
                          %mtd
                            %mi Hom
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi U
                            %mo ,
                            %mi Y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    Hom(U,X) &amp;\stackrel{id}{\longrightarrow}&amp; Hom(U,X)
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{Hom(U,f)}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{Hom(U,f)}}
                    \\\
                    Hom(U,Y) &amp;\stackrel{id}{\longrightarrow}&amp; Hom(U,Y)
                    }
                    \\,,
            %p
              which is trivially a pullback. Consider then objects of the form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ×
                    %mi 𝔻
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \times \mathbb{D}
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔻
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{D}
              the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+interval"} infinitesimal interval
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#NatureOfTheModalitiesOnCahiersTopos"}
              and by prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TangentBundlesAsInternalHoms"}
              they all giving pullbacks is equivalent to the diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi T
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi d
                                  %mi f
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi T
                            %mi Y
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    T X &amp;\stackrel{}{\longrightarrow}&amp; X
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{d f}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    T Y &amp;\stackrel{}{\longrightarrow}&amp; Y
                    }
            %p
              being a pullback. By prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocalDiffeosDetectedByPullbackOfTangentBundle"}
              this is already equivalent to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              being a local diffeomorphism.
            %p
              But local diffeomorphisms of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
              (as opposed to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formally+%C3%A9tale+morphisms"} formally étale morphisms
              of
              = succeed "!)" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/schemes"} schemes
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+morphisms"} étale morphisms
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+neighbourhood"} infinitesimal neighbourhood
              around each point, but the whole
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/germ"} germ
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi InfPoint
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi FormalSmoothCartSp
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi FormalSmooth
                    %mn 0
                    %mi Type
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D \in InfPoint \hookrightarrow FormalSmoothCartSp \hookrightarrow FormalSmooth0Type
              any object, also the image of the diagram under
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo ×
                    %mi D
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(U \times D,-)
              gives a pullback.
          %p
            Given prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TraditionalLocalDiffeosByModality"}
            it makes sense to say
          #LocalDiffeosGenerallyInCahiersTopos.num_defn
            %h6#definition_6 Definition
            %p
              A morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X\to Y
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi FormalSmooth
                    %mn 0
                    %mi Type
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} FormalSmooth0Type
              is a
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+diffeomorphism"} local diffeomorphism
              (or
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formally+%C3%A9tale+morphism"} formally étale morphism
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} naturality sqare
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+a+monad"} unit
              of its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+shape+modality"} infinitesimal shape modality
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℑ
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi ℑ
                                  %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℑ
                            %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X &amp;\stackrel{}{\longrightarrow}&amp; \Im X
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{f}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\Im f}}
                    \\\
                    Y &amp;\stackrel{}{\longrightarrow}&amp; \Im Y
                    }
            %p
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              diagram.
          %h5#SmoothManifold Smooth manifolds
          %p
            With the (re-)formulation of local diffeomorphisms between smooth manifolds and their generalization to maps of smooth sets by prop.
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocalDiffeosGenerallyInCahiersTopos"}
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+sets"} smooth sets
          #ManifoldsAsEtaleGroupoids.num_defn
            %h6#definitionproposition Definition/Proposition
            %p
              For
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n\in \mathbb{N}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              is an object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi FormalSmooth
                    %mn 0
                    %mi Type
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in FormalSmooth0Type
              such that there exists a morphisms of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo =
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mi i
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\underset{i }{\coprod} U_i
                    \\stackrel{=}{\to}
                    \\underset{i }{\coprod} \mathbb{R}^n
                    \\longrightarrow
                    X
            %p which is
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  an
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphism"} epimorphism
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+diffeomorphism"} local diffeomorphism
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocalDiffeosGenerallyInCahiersTopos"}
          .proof
            %h6#proof_4 Proof
            %p
              A quick abstract way to prove this, for which however at this point we have not provided all the ingredients yet, is to observe that the map being an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-epimorphism"} 1-epimorphism
              makes it equivalent to its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+nerve"} Cech nerve
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid+object+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} groupoid object
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+groupoid"} étale groupoid
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+groupoid"} Cech groupoid
              of that smooth manifold
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ,
                        %mi j
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %munder
                      %mo ×
                      %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi j
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo ⟶
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\underset{i,j}{\coprod}  U_i \underset{X}{\times} U_j
                    \\stackrel{\longrightarrow}{\longrightarrow}
                    \\underset{i}{\coprod} U_i
            %p with respect to the cover that we started with above.
          %h5#FrameBundleTraditional Frame bundles
          %blockquote
            %p the following is some semi-traditional basic discussion. Need to see what to do with this here.
          %p
            On each overlap
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo ∩
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi j
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i \cap U_j
            of two charts, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+derivatives"} partial derivatives
            of the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinate+transformations"} coordinate transformations
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mi j
                  %mo ∘
                  %msubsup
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mi i
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo ∩
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi j
                  %mo ⊂
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\phi_j\circ \phi_i^{-1}
                  \:
                  U_i \cap U_j \subset \mathbb{R}^n \to \mathbb{R}^n
          %p
            form the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacobian+matrix"} Jacobian matrix
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi λ
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mi j
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi μ
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mi μ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mrow
                    %mo [
                    %mfrac
                      %mi d
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %msup
                          %mi x
                          %mi ν
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mi j
                    %mo ∘
                    %msubsup
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mi i
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mi μ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ]
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo ∩
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi j
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi GL
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  ((\lambda_{i j})^{\mu}{}_{\mu})
                  \\coloneqq
                  \\left[\frac{d}{d x^\nu} \phi_j \circ \phi_i^{-1} (x^\mu)
                  \\right]
                  \:
                  U_i \cap U_j
                  \\to
                  GL_n
          %p
            with values in invertible
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matrices"} matrices
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+linear+group"} general linear group
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(n)
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+rule"} chain rule
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matrix+product"} matrix product
            equations
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi λ
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mi j
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi μ
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mi λ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi λ
                    %mrow
                      %mi j
                      %mi k
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi λ
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mi ν
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi λ
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mi k
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi μ
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mi ν
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (\lambda_{i j})^\mu{}_\lambda (\lambda_{j k})^\lambda{}_{\nu}
                  \=
                  (\lambda_{i k})^\mu{}_{\nu}
                  \\,,
          %p (here and in the following sums over an index appearing upstairs and downstairs are explicit)
          %p hence the equation
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi λ
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mi j
                  %mo ⋅
                  %msub
                    %mi λ
                    %mrow
                      %mi j
                      %mi k
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi λ
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\lambda_{i j} \cdot \lambda_{j k} = \lambda_{i k}
          %p
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo ∩
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi j
                  %mo ∩
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi k
                  %mo ,
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(U_i \cap U_j \cap U_k, GL(n))
            of smooth
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(n)
          %p
            This is the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
              condition
            for a smooth
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+cohomology"} Cech cocycle
            in degree 1 with coefficients in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(n)
            (precisely: with coefficients in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
            with values in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(n)
            ). We write
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi λ
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ∈
                  %msubsup
                    %mi H
                    %mi smooth
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi GL
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [(\lambda_{i j})] \in H^1_{smooth}(X, GL_n)
                  \\,.
          %p
            Formulated as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+groupoids"} smooth groupoids
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                itself is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoid"} Lie groupoid
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mo ⟶
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X \stackrel{\longrightarrow}{\longrightarrow} X)
                with trivial morphism structure;
            %li
              %p
                from the atlas
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \to X\}
                we get the corresponding
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+groupoid"} Cech groupoid
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo ,
                          %mi j
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo ∩
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi j
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mo ⟶
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                        %mi i
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mrow
                        %mo {
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi x
                                %mo ,
                                %mi j
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mo ↗
                              %mtd
                                %mo =
                              %mtd
                                %mo ↘
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi x
                                %mo ,
                                %mi i
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mo →
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi x
                                %mo ,
                                %mi k
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi for
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                        %mo ∩
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi j
                        %mo ∩
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi k
                        %mo }
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      C(\{U_i\}) =
                      (\coprod_{i, j} U_i \cap U_j \stackrel{\longrightarrow}{\longrightarrow} \coprod_i U_i)
                      \=
                      \\left\{
                      \\array{
                      \&amp;&amp; (x,j)
                      \\\
                      \&amp; \nearrow &amp;=&amp; \searrow
                      \\\
                      (x,i) &amp;&amp;\to&amp;&amp; (x,k)
                      }
                      \\;\;\;
                      for\, x \in U_i \cap U_j \cap U_k
                      \\right\}
                      \\,,
              %p
                whose objects are the points in the atlas, with morphisms identifying lifts of a point in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                to different charts of the atlas;
          %p
            The above situation is neatly encoded in the existence of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
            of Lie groupoids of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                          %msub
                            %mi U
                            %mi i
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi τ
                                %mi X
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi GL
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo .
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mo ≃
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  C(\{U_i\}) &amp;\stackrel{\tau_X}{\longrightarrow}&amp; \mathbf{B} GL(n).
                  \\\
                  {}^{\mathllap{\simeq}}\downarrow
                  \\\
                  X
                  }
                  \\,,
          %p where
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the left morphism is
                = succeed "-wise" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stalk"} stalk
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neighbourhoods"} neighbourhoods
                of each point) an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+groupoids"} equivalence of groupoids
                (we make this more precise in a moment);
            %li
              %p
                the horizontal functor
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi τ
                        %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau_X
                has as components the functions
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi λ
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mi j
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda_{i j}
                and its functoriality is the cocycle condition
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi λ
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mi j
                        %mo ⋅
                        %msub
                          %mi λ
                          %mrow
                            %mi j
                            %mi k
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi λ
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda_{i j} \cdot \lambda_{j k} = \lambda_{i k}
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} transformation
            of smooth functors
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi λ
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ⇒
                  %msub
                    %mi λ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda_1 \Rightarrow \lambda_2 : C(\{U_i\}) \to \mathbf{B} GL(n)
            is precisely a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coboundary"} coboundary
            between two such cocycles.
          %p
            This defines a morphism of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+groupoids"} smooth groupoids
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi τ
                    %mi X
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\tau_X \;\colon\; X \to \mathbf{B}GL(n)
                  \\,.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber"} homotopy fiber
            of this map is a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(n)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
            called the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/frame+bundle"} frame bundle
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associated+bundle"} associated bundle
            via the canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation"} representation
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(n)
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundle"} tangent bundle
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  T X \to X
                  \\,.
          %h4#tale_groupoids Étale groupoids
          %p
            We now lift the
            %a{:href => "#ModelLayerManifolds"} above
            discussion of smooth manifolds inside
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+sets"} smooth sets
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+shape+modality"} infinitesimal shape modality
            from the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+sets"} smooth sets
            to that of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+groupoids"} smooth groupoids
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+groupoids"} smooth groupoids
            see the relevant discussions at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+smooth+homotopy+types"} geometry of physics – smooth homotopy types
          %h5#formal_smooth_groupoids Formal smooth groupoids
          %p
            In view of the refinement of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+sets"} smooth sets
            on the one hand to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+smooth+sets"} formal smooth sets
            and on the other hand to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+groupoid"} smooth groupoid
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+smooth+groupoids"} formal smooth groupoids
          %p This proceeds essentially verbatim to the previous definitions
          #FormalSmoothGroupoids.num_defn
            %h6#definition_7 Definition
            %p
              A
              %em pre-formal smooth groupoid
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoids"} groupoids
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi FormalSmoothCartSp
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} FormalSmoothCartSp
            %p Write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi FormalSmooth
                    %mn 1
                    %mi Type
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mi lwhe
                    %mi PreFormalSmooth
                    %mn 1
                    %mi Type
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    FormalSmooth1Type \coloneqq L_{lwhe} PreFormalSmooth1Type
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%282%2C1%29-category"} (2,1)-category
              which is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+localization"} simplicial localization
              at the local weak equivalences.
          %p (…)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi Smooth
                          %mn 1
                          %mi Type
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mover
                              %mover
                                %mo ⟵
                                %mo ↪
                              %mo ⟵
                            %mo ↪
                        %mtd
                          %mi FormalSmooth
                          %mn 1
                          %mi Type
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi Smooth
                          %mn 0
                          %mi Type
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mover
                              %mover
                                %mo ⟵
                                %mo ↪
                              %mo ⟵
                            %mo ↪
                        %mtd
                          %mi FormalSmooth
                          %mn 0
                          %mi Type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  Smooth1Type &amp;
                  \\stackrel{\hookrightarrow}{\stackrel{\longleftarrow}{\stackrel{\hookrightarrow}{\longleftarrow}}}
                  \&amp; FormalSmooth1Type
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  Smooth0Type
                  \&amp;
                  \\stackrel{\hookrightarrow}{\stackrel{\longleftarrow}{\stackrel{\hookrightarrow}{\longleftarrow}}}
                  \&amp;
                  FormalSmooth0Type
                  }
          %p
            We may now directy adapt the definition of local diffeos as in def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocalDiffeosGenerallyInCahiersTopos"}
            simply by generalizing
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/0-types"} 0-types
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-types"} 1-types
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullbacks"} pullbacks
            to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullbacks"} homotopy pullbacks
          #LocalDiffeosGenerallyInFormalSmooth1Types.num_defn
            %h6#definition_8 Definition
            %p
              A morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X\to Y
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi FormalSmooth
                      %mn 1
                      %mi Type
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} FormalSmooth1Type
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FormalSmoothGroupoids"}
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+diffeomorphism"} local diffeomorphism
              (or
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formally+%C3%A9tale+morphism"} formally étale morphism
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} naturality sqare
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+a+monad"} unit
              of its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+shape+modality"} infinitesimal shape modality
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℑ
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi ℑ
                                  %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℑ
                            %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X &amp;\stackrel{}{\longrightarrow}&amp; \Im X
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{f}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\Im f}}
                    \\\
                    Y &amp;\stackrel{}{\longrightarrow}&amp; \Im Y
                    }
            %p
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
              diagram.
          %h5#EtaleLieGroupoids Étale Lie groupoids
          %p
            The traditional definition of smooth
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+groupoids"} étale groupoids
            is the following:
          #EtaleGroupoidTraditional.num_defn
            %h6#definition_9 Definition
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoid"} Lie groupoid
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒢
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G}_\bullet
              is
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+groupoid"} étale
              if its target map
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒢
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒢
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    t \colon \mathcal{G}_1 \longrightarrow \mathcal{G}_0
            %p
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+diffeomorphism"} local diffeomorphism
          #ImplicitConditionsInEtaleGroupoidDef.num_remark
            %h6#remark_4 Remark
            %p
              The condition in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EtaleGroupoidTraditional"}
              implies that all the other structure maps are local diffeomorphisms, too:
            %p
              Inversion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒢
                      %mn 1
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒢
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^{-1}\colon \mathcal{G}_1\stackrel{\simeq}{\to} \mathcal{G}_1
              is even a global
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphism"} diffeomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo =
                    %mi t
                    %mo ∘
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s = t \circ (-)^{-1}
              is the composite of two local diffeos and as such itself a local diffeo.
            %p
              The identity-assigning map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒢
                      %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒢
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \colon \mathcal{G}_0 \to \mathcal{G}_1
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
              of a local diffeo (either
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
              or
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi t
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
            %p
              The two projections out of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒢
                      %mn 1
                    %munder
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒢
                          %mn 0
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒢
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G}_1 \underset{\mathcal{G}_0}{\times} \mathcal{G}_1
              are pullbacks of local diffeos, and hence themselves local diffeos.
          %p We now rephrase this more intrinsically.
          %p
            Given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoid"} Lie groupoid
            we write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒢
                    %mn 0
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi 𝒢
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G}_0 \longrightarrow \mathcal{G}
            for the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiable+stack"} differentiable stack
            with
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/atlas"} atlas
          #EtaleGroupoidByInfinitesimalShape.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_7 Proposition
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoid"} Lie groupoid
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒢
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G}_\bullet
              is an
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+groupoid"} étale groupoid
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EtaleGroupoidTraditional"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔾
                      %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒢
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{G}_0 \to \mathcal{G}
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+diffeomorphism"} local diffeomorphism
              of smooth groupoids, def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocalDiffeosGenerallyInFormalSmooth1Types"}
              in that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi 𝒢
                              %mn 0
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℑ
                            %msub
                              %mi 𝒢
                              %mn 0
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi 𝒢
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℑ
                            %mi 𝒢
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\mathcal{G}_0 &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; \Im \mathcal{G}_0
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\mathcal{G} &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; \Im \mathcal{G}
                    }
            %p
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
              diagram of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+smooth+groupoids"} formal smooth groupoids
          .proof
            %h6#proof_5 Proof
            %p
              We compute the homotopy pulback by fibrant presentation of the morphism on the right, via the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/factorization+lemma"} factorization lemma
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi 𝒢
                              %mn 0
                            %munder
                              %mo ×
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi 𝒢
                                  %mo •
                            %msubsup
                              %mi 𝒢
                              %mo •
                              %mi I
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℑ
                            %msub
                              %mi 𝒢
                              %mn 0
                            %munder
                              %mo ×
                              %mrow
                                %mi ℑ
                                %msub
                                  %mi 𝒢
                                  %mo •
                            %mi ℑ
                            %msubsup
                              %mi 𝒢
                              %mo •
                              %mi I
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi 𝒢
                              %mo •
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℑ
                            %msub
                              %mi 𝒢
                              %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\mathcal{G}_0 \underset{\mathcal{G}_\bullet}{\times} \mathcal{G}^I_\bullet  &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; \Im \mathcal{G}_0 \underset{\Im\mathcal{G}_\bullet}{\times} \Im\mathcal{G}^I_\bullet
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\mathcal{G}_\bullet &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; \Im \mathcal{G}_\bullet
                    }
            %p
              Inspection shows that in degree 0 this diagram is just the naturality square of the
              = succeed "-unit" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℑ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Im
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi t
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒢
                        %mn 1
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒢
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t\colon \mathcal{G}_1 \to \mathcal{G}_0
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TraditionalLocalDiffeosByModality"}
              this is a pullback in degree-0 precisely already if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒢
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G}_\bullet
              is étale. By remark
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ImplicitConditionsInEtaleGroupoidDef"}
              this implies that the projection
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒢
                      %mn 1
                    %munder
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒢
                          %mn 0
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒢
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒢
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_2 \colon \mathcal{G}_1\underset{\mathcal{G}_0}{\times}\mathcal{G}_1 \to \mathcal{G}_1
              is a local diffeo, and that is equivalent to the above diagram being a pullback in degree 1.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_5 Remark
            %p
              In view of def./prop.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ManifoldsAsEtaleGroupoids"}
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EtaleGroupoidByInfinitesimalShape"}
              gives that
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+groupoids"} étale groupoids
              are precisely the “1-higher manifolds”. For historical reasons this kind of statement is more prominent in the context of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+geometry"} algebraic geometry
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Artin+stacks"} Artin stacks
              (in particular
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Deligne-Mumford+stacks"} Deligne-Mumford stacks
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+schemes"} derived schemes
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_6 Remark
            %p
              Another point that prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EtaleGroupoidByInfinitesimalShape"}
              makes maybe more manifest is that the traditional definition
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EtaleGroupoidTraditional"}
              makes a silent assumption that one may want to make explicit: it characterizes a Lie groupoid as
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+Lie+groupoid"} étale
              = succeed "." do
                %em relative to a manifold
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒢
                      %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒢
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G}_0 \to \mathcal{G}
              is an étale atlas of a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiable+stack"} differentiable stack
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒢
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\mathbb{R}^n \simeq U_i \to \mathcal{G}_0\}
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
              of the smooth manifold
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒢
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G}_0
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ≔
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mi i
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒢
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi 𝒢
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    U \coloneqq \underset{i}{\coprod} \mathbb{R}^n \longrightarrow \mathcal{G}_0
                    \\longrightarrow
                    \\mathcal{G}
            %p
              is an étale atlas. This means that the étale nature of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒢
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G}_\bullet
              is really with respect to the chosen model space
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo ≔
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    V \coloneqq \mathbb{R}^n
                    \\,.
            %p
              One way to make this explicit in the more intrinsic diagrammatic formulation that we are discussing here is to say that we have a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correspondence"} correspondence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi U
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↙
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↘
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi V
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \&amp;&amp; U
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \swarrow &amp;&amp; \searrow
                    \\\
                    V &amp;&amp; &amp;&amp; X
                    }
            %p where
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  both morphisms are
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+diffeomorphisms"} local diffeomorphisms
                  of smooth groupoids, def.
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocalDiffeosGenerallyInFormalSmooth1Types"}
              %li
                %p
                  the right morphism in addition is an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+epimorphism"} effective epimorphism
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-epimorphism"}> 1-epimorphism
                  ).
            %p
              Jointly this says that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \to X
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/atlas"} atlas
              which is étale relative to the model space
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %p
              This perspective leads to the general abstract definition of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/V-manifolds"} V-manifolds
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+differential+geometry"} higher differential geometry
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} étale ∞-groupoids
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#VManifolds"} below
          %h3#semantics_layer Semantics Layer
          %h4#differential_cohesion Differential cohesion
          %p
            In the above discussion we found an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+quadruple"} adjoint quadruple
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AdjointQuadrupleOnFormalSmoothSets"}
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+smooth+sets"} formal smooth sets
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
            entirely in terms of the induced
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            which we called the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+shape+modality"} infinitesimal shape modality
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℑ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Im
          %p
            One may hence turn this around and regard any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos
            that is equipped with an adjoint quadruple inclusion in this way as a formal context for manifold theory (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elasticity"}> elasticity
            ”).
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_10 Definition
            %p
              Given a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
              then the structure of
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohesion"} differential cohesion
              on it is a choice of sub-topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo !
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                      %mi ℜ
                    %mo ↪
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_! \colon \mathbf{H}_{\Re} \hookrightarrow \mathbf{H}
              such that the inclusion extends to an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+quadruple"} adjoint quadruple
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                      %mi ℜ
                    %mover
                      %mover
                        %mover
                          %munder
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mrow
                              %msup
                                %mi i
                                %mo !
                          %mover
                            %mo ↪
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi i
                                %mo *
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟵
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi i
                              %mo *
                      %mover
                        %mo ↪
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi i
                            %mo !
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{H}_{\Re}
                    \\stackrel{\overset{i_!}{\hookrightarrow}}{\stackrel{\overset{i^\ast}{\longleftarrow}}{\stackrel{\overset{i_\ast}{\hookrightarrow}}{\underset{i^!}{\longrightarrow}}}}
                    \\mathbf{H}
            %p
              and such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo !
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_!
              preserves finite products. Given this then we write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℜ
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi ℑ
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi &amp;
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mover
                      %mover
                        %munder
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi i
                              %mo !
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟵
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi i
                              %mo *
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi i
                            %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                      %mi ℜ
                    %mover
                      %mover
                        %munder
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi i
                              %mo *
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟵
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi i
                              %mo *
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi i
                            %mo !
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\Re \dashv \Im \dashv \&amp;)
                    \\;\colon\;
                    \\mathbf{H}
                    \\stackrel{\overset{i^\ast}{\longrightarrow}}{\stackrel{\overset{i_\ast}{\longleftarrow}}{\underset{i^!}{\longrightarrow}}}
                    \\mathbf{H}_{\Re}
                    \\stackrel{\overset{i_!}{\longrightarrow}}{\stackrel{\overset{i^\ast}{\longleftarrow}}{\underset{i_\ast}{\longrightarrow}}}
                    \\mathbf{H}
            %p
              for the induced
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+triple"} adjoint triple
              of (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-comonad"}> co
              \-)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-monads"} (∞,1)-monads
              induced from the four
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functors"} (∞,1)-functors
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℜ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Re
                  –
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduction+modality"} reduction modality
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℑ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Im
                  –
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+shape+modality"} infinitesimal shape modality
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi &amp;
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \&amp;
                  –
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+flat+modality"} infinitesimal flat modality
          %h4#VManifolds
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            \-Manifolds
          #LocalDiffeomorphismsInDifferentialCohesion.num_defn
            %h6#definition_11 Definition
            %p
              Given
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X,Y\in \mathbf{H}
              then a morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \;\colon\; X\longrightarrow Y
              is a
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+diffeomorphism"} local diffeomorphism
              if its naturality square of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+shape+modality"} infinitesimal shape modality
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℑ
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi ℑ
                                  %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℑ
                            %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; \Im X
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{f}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\Im f}}
                    \\\
                    Y &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; \Im Y
                    }
            %p
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
              square.
          %p
            Let now
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo ∈
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \in \mathbf{H}
            be given, equipped with the structure of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-group"}> ∞-group
            ).
          #VManifold.num_defn
            %h6#definition_12 Definition
            %p
              A
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/V-manifold"} V-manifold
              is an
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in \mathbf{H}
              such that there exists a
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                  \-
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/atlas"} atlas
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correspondence"} correspondence
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi U
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↙
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↘
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi V
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \&amp;&amp; U
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \swarrow &amp;&amp; \searrow
                    \\\
                    V &amp;&amp; &amp;&amp; X
                    }
            %p
              with both morphisms being
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+diffeomorphisms"} local diffeomorphisms
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocalDiffeomorphismsInDifferentialCohesion"}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphism"} epimorphism
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/atlas"} atlas
          %h4#FrameBundles Frame bundles
          #InfinitesimalDisk.num_defn
            %h6#definition_13 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in \mathbf{H}
              an object and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \colon \ast \to X
              a point, then we say that the
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+neighbourhood"} infinitesimal neighbourhood
                  of
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+disk"} infinitesimal disk
                at
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber"} homotopy fiber
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi 𝔻
                      %mi x
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{D}^X_x
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+a+monad"} unit
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+shape+modality"} infinitesimal shape modality
              at
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mi 𝔻
                              %mi x
                              %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo *
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi x
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} im
                            %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\mathbb{D}^X_x &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; X
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\ast &amp;\stackrel{x}{\longrightarrow}&amp; \im X
                    }
                    \\,.
          #FormalDiskBundle.num_defn
            %h6#definition_14 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              any object in differential cohesion, its
              %em infinitesimal disk bundle
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mi inf
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_{inf} X \to X
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi T
                              %mi inf
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi ev
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi p
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℑ
                            %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    T_{inf} X &amp;\stackrel{ev}{\longrightarrow}&amp; X
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{p}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    X &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; \Im X
                    }
            %p
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+a+monad"} unit
              of its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+shape+modality"} infinitesimal shape modality
              along itself.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_7 Remark
            %p
              By the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting+law"} pasting law
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber"} homotopy fiber
              of the infinitesimal disk bundle, def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FormalDiskBundle"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              is the infinitesimal disk
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi 𝔻
                      %mi x
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{D}^X_x
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              at that point, def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InfinitesimalDisk"}>
              \. Nevertheless, for general
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              the infinitesimal disk bundle need not be an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} fiber ∞-bundle
              with typical fiber (the infinitesimal disks at different points need not be equivalent, and even if they are, the bundle need not be locally trivial). Below in prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FormalDiskBundleOfRegularManifoldsTrivializesOverCover"}
              we see that for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              a
              = succeed "-manifold" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} fiber ∞-bundle
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associated+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} associated ∞-bundle
              to some
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} principal ∞-bundle
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/frame+bundle"} frame bundle
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_8 Remark
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Atiyah+groupoid"} Atiyah groupoid
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mi inf
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_{inf} X
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/jet+groupoid"} jet groupoid
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          #EtalePullbackOfFormalDiskBundleIsFormalDiskBundle.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma Lemma
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ι
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi U
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \iota \colon U \to X
              is a local diffeomorphism, def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocalDiffeomorphismsInDifferentialCohesion"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ι
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mi inf
                    %mi X
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mi inf
                    %mi U
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\iota^\ast T_{inf} X \simeq T_{inf}U
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_6 Proof
            %p
              By the definition of local diffeos and using the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting+law"} pasting law
              we have an equivalence of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting+diagrams"} pasting diagrams
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullbacks"} homotopy pullbacks
              of the following form:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi ι
                              %mo *
                            %msub
                              %mi T
                              %mi inf
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi T
                              %mi inf
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi U
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℑ
                            %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi T
                              %mi inf
                            %mi U
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi U
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi U
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℑ
                            %mi U
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℑ
                            %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\iota^\ast T_{inf} X &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; T_{inf} &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; X
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    U &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; X &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; \Im X
                    }
                    \\;\;\;\;
                    \\simeq
                    \\;\;\;\;
                    \\array{
                    T_{inf} U &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; U &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; X
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    U &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; \Im U &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; \Im X
                    }
          #Framing.num_defn
            %h6#definition_15 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              an object, a
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/framing"} framing
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              is a trivialization of its infinitesimal disk bundle, def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FormalDiskBundle"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝔻
                      %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{D}^V
              – the typical
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+disk"} infinitesimal disk
              or
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+disk"} formal disk
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InfinitesimalDisk"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi T
                              %mi inf
                            %mi V
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi V
                            %mo ×
                            %msup
                              %mi 𝔻
                              %mi n
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↙
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi p
                                    %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi V
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    T_{inf} V &amp;&amp; \stackrel{\simeq}{\longrightarrow} &amp;&amp; V \times \mathbb{D}^n
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow_{\mathrlap{p_1}}
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; V
                    }
                    \\,.
          #GeneralLinearGroup.num_defn
            %h6#definition_16 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              a framed object, def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Framing"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Aut
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝔻
                      %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    GL(V) \coloneqq \mathbf{Aut}(\mathbb{D}^V)
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+%E2%88%9E-group"} automorphism ∞-group
              of its typical
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+disk"} infinitesimal disk
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+disk"} formal disk
          #OrderOfInfinitesimalDisks.num_remark
            %h6#remark_9 Remark
            %p
              When the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+shape+modality"} infinitesimal shape modality
              exhibits first-order infinitesimals, such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔻
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{D}(V)
              is the first order
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+neighbourhood"} infinitesimal neighbourhood
              of a point, then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Aut
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔻
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Aut}(\mathbb{D}(V))
              indeed plays the role of the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+linear+group"} general linear group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝔻
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{D}^n
              is instead a higher order or even the whole
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+neighbourhood"} formal neighbourhood
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(n)
              is rather a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/jet+group"} jet group
              = succeed "-jets" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi GL
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL^k(V)
              We nevertheless stick with the notation “
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(V)
              ” here, consistent with the fact that we have no index on the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+shape+modality"} infinitesimal shape modality
          %p This class of examples of framings is important:
          #DifferentialCohesiveInfinityGroupIsCanonicallyFramed.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_8 Proposition
            %p
              Every differentially cohesive
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-group"} ∞-group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              is canonically framed (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Framing"}
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FormalDiskBundle"}
              is given by the left action of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              on its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+disk"} infinitesimal disk
              at the neutral element:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ev
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mi inf
                    %mi G
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi G
                    %mo ×
                    %msubsup
                      %mi 𝔻
                      %mi e
                      %mi G
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo ⋅
                    %mi G
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    ev \;\colon\; T_{inf}G \simeq G \times \mathbb{D}^G_e \stackrel{\cdot}{\longrightarrow} G
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_7 Proof
            %p
              By the discussion at
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mayer-Vietoris+sequence"} Mayer-Vietoris sequence
              in the section
              %em
                %a{:href => "Mayer-Vietoris%20sequence#OverAGroupObject"} Over an ∞-group
              and using that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+shape+modality"} infinitesimal shape modality
              preserves group structure, the defining
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi T
                        %mi inf
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_{inf} G
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FormalDiskBundle"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi T
                              %mi inf
                            %mi G
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mi 𝔻
                              %mi e
                              %mi G
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mo *
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi G
                            %mo ×
                            %mi G
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo ⋅
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %msup
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                    %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mi G
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℑ
                            %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    T_{inf} G &amp;\stackrel{}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    \\mathbb{D}^G_e
                    \&amp;\stackrel{}{\longrightarrow}&amp; \ast
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp;  \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    G \times G &amp;\stackrel{(-)\cdot (-)^{-1}}{\longrightarrow}&amp; G
                    \&amp;\stackrel{}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    \\Im G
                    }
            %p
              where the right square is the defining pullback for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+disk"} infinitesimal disk
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝔻
                        %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{D}^G
              %a{:href => "Mayer-Vietoris%20sequence#HTTArgumentForPullback"} this proposition
              that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mi inf
                    %mi G
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi G
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝔻
                      %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_{inf} G \simeq G\times \mathbb{D}^G
              and that the top horizontal morphism is as claimed.
          %p
            By lemma
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EtalePullbackOfFormalDiskBundleIsFormalDiskBundle"}
            it follows that:
          #FormalDiskBundleOfRegularManifoldsTrivializesOverCover.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_9 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              a framed object, def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Framing"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a
              = succeed "-manifold," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#VManifold"}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FormalDiskBundle"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              canonically trivializes over any
              = succeed "-cover" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo ←
                    %mi U
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \leftarrow U \rightarrow X
              , i.e. there is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi U
                            %mo ×
                            %msup
                              %mi 𝔻
                              %mi V
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi T
                              %mi inf
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi U
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    U \times \mathbb{D}^V &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; T_{inf} X
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    U &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; X
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              This exhibits
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mi inf
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_{inf} X\to X
              as a
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝔻
                        %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{D}^V
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} fiber ∞-bundle
          #ModulatingMapOfFormalDiskBundle.num_prop
            %h6#remark_10 Remark
            %p
              By
              %a{:href => "fiber+infinity-bundle#Properties"} this discussion
              this fiber
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} fiber ∞-bundle
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associated+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} associated ∞-bundle
              of an essentially uniquely determined
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Aut
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝔻
                        %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Aut}(\mathbb{D}^V)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} principal ∞-bundle
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Fr
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Fr(X)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
              diagram of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi T
                              %mi inf
                            %mi X
                            %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                            %mi Fr
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %munder
                              %mo ×
                              %mrow
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mi Aut
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msup
                                  %mi 𝔻
                                  %mi V
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %msup
                              %mi 𝔻
                              %mi V
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi V
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi Aut
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi 𝔻
                              %mi V
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi Aut
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi 𝔻
                              %mi V
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    T_{inf} X \simeq
                    \&amp;
                    Fr(X) \underset{\mathbf{Aut}(\mathbb{D}^V)}{\times} \mathbb{D}^V
                    \&amp;\longrightarrow&amp;
                    V//\mathbf{Aut}(\mathbb{D}^V)
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \&amp; X &amp;\stackrel{}{\longrightarrow}&amp; \mathbf{B}\mathbf{Aut}(\mathbb{D}^V)
                    }
                    \\,.
          #FrameBundleMap.num_defn
            %h6#definition_17 Definition
            %p
              Given a
              = succeed "-manifold" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#VManifold"}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Framing"}
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/frame+bundle"} frame bundle
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Fr
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    Fr(X)
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow
                    \\\
                    X
                    }
            %p
              is the
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi GL
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(V)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} principal ∞-bundle
              given by prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FormalDiskBundleOfRegularManifoldsTrivializesOverCover"}
              via remark
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ModulatingMapOfFormalDiskBundle"}
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_11 Remark
            %p
              As in remark
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OrderOfInfinitesimalDisks"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+order+frame+bundles"} higher order frame bundles
              with the order implicit in the nature of the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+shape+modality"} infinitesimal shape modality
          #FrameBundlesFunctorial.num_remark
            %h6#remark_12 Remark
            %p
              By prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EtalePullbackOfFormalDiskBundleIsFormalDiskBundle"}
              the construction of frame bundles in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FrameBundleMap"}
              is functorial in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formally+%C3%A9tale+maps"} formally étale maps
              between
              = succeed "-manifolds." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
          %p
            This provides all the necessary structure to now set up an axiomatic theory of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-structure"} G-structure
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+Cartan+geometry"} higher Cartan geometry
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+G-structure+and+Cartan+geometry"} geometry of physics – G-structure and Cartan geometry
          %h3#syntax_layer Syntax Layer
          %p
            (…) formulation of the above in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            in
            %a{:href => "#Wellen17"} Wellen 17
            (…)
          %h2#references References
          %p
            The above formulation of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/V-manifolds"} V-manifolds
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohesion"} differential cohesion
            is due to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/differential+cohomology+in+a+cohesive+topos"} dcct
            and
          %ul
            %li#KhavkineSchreiber17
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Igor+Khavkine"}> Igor Khavkine
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Synthetic+variational+calculus"} Synthetic geometry of differential equations: I. Jets and comonad structure
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1701.06238"}> arXiv:1701.06238
              )
          %p
            and the formalization in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Wellen17
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Felix+Wellen"}> Felix Wellen
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/thesis+Wellen"} Formalizing Cartan Geometry in Modal Homotopy Type Theory
